        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3,1)$ and $(-1,-3)$.",
          "worked": "Since $x\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x-2&=\\frac3x\\\\x^2-2x&=3\\\\x^2-2x-3&=0\\\\(x-3)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=3\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=3$, $y=3-2=1$; for $x=-1$, $y=-1-2=-3$.\nThe intersections are $(3,1)$ and $(-1,-3)$. The hyperbola has asymptotes $x=0$ and $y=0$.",
